---
import '../styles/custom.css';
import '../styles/index-page.css';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ThemeProvider from '../components/ThemeProvider.astro';

const UPDATED = 'April 29, 2026';
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Privacy · Froglet</title>
<meta name="description" content="Froglet privacy posture for the public website, hosted proof trial, and ChatGPT app surface." />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://froglet.dev/privacy/" />
<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="Froglet" />
<meta property="og:title" content="Privacy · Froglet" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Froglet privacy posture for the public website, hosted proof trial, and ChatGPT app surface." />
<meta property="og:url" content="https://froglet.dev/privacy/" />
<meta property="og:image" content="https://froglet.dev/og/home.png" />
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Privacy · Froglet" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Froglet privacy posture for the public website, hosted proof trial, and ChatGPT app surface." />
<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://froglet.dev/og/home.png" />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
<ThemeProvider />
</head>
<body data-screen-label="Privacy">
<SiteHeader currentPath={Astro.url.pathname} />
<main class="froglet-home-main">
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Public proof, <em>local secrets.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Froglet is an Apache-2.0 open source protocol. This page explains the
      privacy boundary for the public website, hosted proof trial, and ChatGPT
      app surface. Last updated: {UPDATED}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block privacy-block">
    <span class="eyebrow">Short version</span>
    <h2>Do not paste secrets into hosted demos or ChatGPT.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      The hosted proof is designed for public demo inputs. Local private keys,
      Lightning macaroons, Stripe keys, x402 credentials, card data, production
      API tokens, and private datasets should be configured only in your own
      local or self-hosted environment.
    </p>

    <div class="entry-grid privacy-grid">
      <article class="entry-card">
        <div class="entry-num">01 · website</div>
        <h3>Public docs and pages</h3>
        <p>
          <code class="inline">froglet.dev</code> serves public documentation
          and marketing pages. The hosting layer may keep standard request logs
          needed for security, abuse prevention, debugging, and reliability.
          The site does not ask for account signup or payment details.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="entry-card">
        <div class="entry-num">02 · hosted proof</div>
        <h3>Anonymous demo sessions</h3>
        <p>
          <code class="inline">try.froglet.dev</code> can mint short-lived
          anonymous sessions and write demo descriptor, offer, deal, and
          receipt artifacts for public free <code class="inline">demo.*</code>
          services. Those artifacts are proof material, not private storage.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="entry-card">
        <div class="entry-num">03 · ChatGPT app</div>
        <h3>Evidence-first tools</h3>
        <p>
          The Froglet ChatGPT app can call
          <code class="inline">run_hosted_proof</code>,
          <code class="inline">plan_local_install</code>, and
          <code class="inline">explain_use_case</code>. It should use fixed
          public demo inputs by default, explain boundaries, and never request
          private credentials inside ChatGPT.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="entry-card">
        <div class="entry-num">04 · local mode</div>
        <h3>User-controlled configuration</h3>
        <p>
          Local install plans tell you which secrets or wallets a rail requires,
          but those values belong in your shell, config files, keychain, or
          self-hosted node. They should not be pasted into the hosted app.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <span class="eyebrow">Data by tool</span>
    <h2>What the app tools process.</h2>
    <div class="privacy-list">
      <div>
        <h3><code class="inline">run_hosted_proof</code></h3>
        <p>
          Creates an anonymous hosted trial session, discovers public demo
          services, runs <code class="inline">demo.add</code>, optionally runs
          a fixed public witness/hash follow-up against
          <code class="inline">https://example.com/</code>, and reads the public
          artifact feed. It should not use private user files unless a future
          local/self-hosted flow is explicitly configured.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3><code class="inline">plan_local_install</code></h3>
        <p>
          Uses install preferences such as target agent, Docker/source/binary
          footprint, Tor or clearnet, and payment rail choice. It returns a
          plan; it does not run shell commands and does not need your secrets.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3><code class="inline">explain_use_case</code></h3>
        <p>
          Uses only the project summary you provide in the current conversation.
          It does not inspect private repositories, local files, browser tabs,
          credentials, or production systems.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <span class="eyebrow">Retention and sharing</span>
    <h2>Public artifacts are intentionally auditable.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Froglet receipts and feed artifacts are designed to be verifiable later.
      Hosted demo artifacts may remain visible as part of the public proof feed.
      Froglet does not sell personal data. If you need deletion, correction, or
      privacy support, open a GitHub issue or contact the maintainer through
      <a href="https://armanas.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">armanas.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter />
</main>
</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  .privacy-block {
    padding-top: 24px;
  }

  .privacy-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .privacy-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .privacy-list > div {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .privacy-list h3 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--fg1);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .privacy-list p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .privacy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
